  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 128000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "ECS4120 Series datasheet R16 (EC-DS-0324-R16, 2024-03-12) prints 128 Gbps switching capacity and 95 Mpps forwarding rate for the ECS4120-28T: 24x 1G + 4x 10G = 64 Gbps of port rate, so the quoted capacity is the full-duplex aggregate, not a cap. https://www.edge-core.com/download/ecs4120-series-ds-r16/?wpdmdl=1696"
  },
  "notes": "Port census from ECS4120 Series datasheet R16 (EC-DS-0324-R16, 2024-03-12) (https://www.edge-core.com/download/ecs4120-series-ds-r16/?wpdmdl=1696): RJ-45 10/100/1000BASE-T 24, SFP+ 10 Gigabit uplink 4, GE out-of-band management port No, RJ-45 console port 1. The four SFP+ cages also take 1G modules (the datasheet lists 1000BASE-SX/LX/LHX/ZX support there), so each carries speedCaps [1000, 10000]. Flash 256 MB, DRAM 512 MB, MAC table 16 K, jumbo 9 KB, max system power 20 W, 100-240 VAC, 44 x 22 x 4.4 cm, 2.35 kg, fanless. No PoE on any port: the datasheet prints No for 802.3af, 802.3at, dynamic power allocation and PoE budget. Routing is IPv4/IPv6 static route plus RIP v1/v2, and the DHCP server (8 pools, 512 addresses) is what the dhcp-server capability rests on. Software: ECS4120 FW V1.2.2.30, posted with the ECS4120 series R16 datasheet on the product download list; the u-boot upgrade v2.0.0.2 is a separate image. CLI reference, port naming Eth 1/1 - Eth 1/28: https://www.edge-core.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/ECS4120-Series_CLI-R06_20251014.pdf."
